64.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T13:54:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135112722,imgsize-798435.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Beacon of hope': Polish PM Donald Tusk hails ties with India, calls PM Modi a 'friend']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/beacon-of-hope-polish-pm-donald-tusk-hails-ties-with-india-calls-pm-modi-a-friend/articleshow/135112511.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135112511.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk visited India to strengthen bilateral cooperation between India and Poland. He highlighted the absence of conflicts of interest and shared values between the two nations. Both leaders discussed expanding economic opportunities through the India-European Union Free Trade Agreement. Tusk emphasized the positive economic developments achieved by Poland and India over the last 35 years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/beacon-of-hope-polish-pm-donald-tusk-hails-ties-with-india-calls-pm-modi-a-friend/articleshow/135112511.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/beacon-of-hope-polish-pm-donald-tusk-hails-ties-with-india-calls-pm-modi-a-friend/articleshow/135112511.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T13:54:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135112635,imgsize-149124.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1 Indian killed, 2 injured in Dammam airport attack in Saudi Arabia]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-indian-killed-2-injured-in-dammam-airport-attack-in-saudi-arabia/articleshow/135112073.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135112073.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-indian-killed-2-injured-in-dammam-airport-attack-in-saudi-arabia/articleshow/135112073.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-indian-killed-2-injured-in-dammam-airport-attack-in-saudi-arabia/articleshow/135112073.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T13:25:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135112125,imgsize-75738.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['You want to protect infiltrators' votes': Amit Shah's sharp attack on Rahul Gandhi over 'vote theft' claims]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/you-want-to-protect-infiltrators-votes-amit-shahs-sharp-attack-on-rahul-gandhi-over-vote-theft-claims/articleshow/135111599.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135111599.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/you-want-to-protect-infiltrators-votes-amit-shahs-sharp-attack-on-rahul-gandhi-over-vote-theft-claims/articleshow/135111599.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/you-want-to-protect-infiltrators-votes-amit-shahs-sharp-attack-on-rahul-gandhi-over-vote-theft-claims/articleshow/135111599.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T13:08:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135112150,imgsize-835507.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Told them to give it to me in writing': Raihan Vadra recounts how events unfolded before photos were taken down at Bikaner House exhibition]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/told-them-to-give-it-to-me-in-writing-raihan-vadra-recounts-how-events-unfolded-before-photos-were-taken-down-at-bikaner-house-exhibition/articleshow/135111665.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135111665.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Raihan Vadra's photography exhibition, No Idea Is Fine, allegedly faced turmoil at Bikaner House when management objected hours before its start, claiming venue policy violations. While Vadra proposed removing select images, the officials demanded the removal of all 70 photographs, including those depicting the Indian national flag. This sparked outrage among Congress members, igniting debates about censorship and the value of artistic freedom.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/told-them-to-give-it-to-me-in-writing-raihan-vadra-recounts-how-events-unfolded-before-photos-were-taken-down-at-bikaner-house-exhibition/articleshow/135111665.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/told-them-to-give-it-to-me-in-writing-raihan-vadra-recounts-how-events-unfolded-before-photos-were-taken-down-at-bikaner-house-exhibition/articleshow/135111665.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T13:08:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135111757,imgsize-827899.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[State by state, some SIR hurdles are falling]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/state-by-state-some-sir-hurdles-are-falling/articleshow/135110737.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135110737.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[States in India are currently reforming voter registration processes by allowing broader document categories for eligibility. Booth-level officers are actively visiting homes to assist voters left out during revisions. Many regions report that discrepancies are being resolved with less bureaucratic procedures. Voter engagement has improved significantly compared to previous years through various initiatives. The overall aim is to facilitate a smoother registration process for all eligible citizens.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/state-by-state-some-sir-hurdles-are-falling/articleshow/135110737.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/state-by-state-some-sir-hurdles-are-falling/articleshow/135110737.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T12:49:16+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135111010,imgsize-179280.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[EC announces bypoll for Madhya Pradesh Rajya Sabha seat vacated by L Murugan]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-announces-bypoll-for-madhya-pradesh-rajya-sabha-seat-vacated-by-l-murugan/articleshow/135109367.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135109367.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-announces-bypoll-for-madhya-pradesh-rajya-sabha-seat-vacated-by-l-murugan/articleshow/135109367.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-announces-bypoll-for-madhya-pradesh-rajya-sabha-seat-vacated-by-l-murugan/articleshow/135109367.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T11:36:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135109378,imgsize-50354.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Finding a place to belong’: Sonia Gandhi makes Instagram debut, shares first look of memoir]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/finding-a-place-to-belong-sonia-gandhi-makes-instagram-debut-shares-first-look-of-memoir/articleshow/135108732.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135108732.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonia Gandhi has joined Instagram to share the first look of her upcoming memoir titled 'Belonging: A Journey of Love'. The memoir will be released internationally on November 10 and recounts her personal journey from Italy to India. It includes reflections on her relationship with Rajiv Gandhi and family tragedies. Due to a publishing dispute in India, HarperCollins India will now publish the domestic edition.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/finding-a-place-to-belong-sonia-gandhi-makes-instagram-debut-shares-first-look-of-memoir/articleshow/135108732.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/finding-a-place-to-belong-sonia-gandhi-makes-instagram-debut-shares-first-look-of-memoir/articleshow/135108732.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T11:31:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135109243,imgsize-806514.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[INDIA bloc huddle: Leaders to meet virtually on CEC row; SIR irregularities on agenda]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-bloc-huddle-leaders-to-meet-virtually-on-cec-row-sir-irregularities-on-agenda/articleshow/135107949.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135107949.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[INDIA bloc leaders, including Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge, will meet via video conferencing on Thursday. They will strategize regarding the Election Commission’s actions surrounding the electoral rolls. Opposition leaders have accused the Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar of irregularities and demanded his resignation. The bloc plans to continue its campaign against perceived threats to democratic institutions and has submitted a memorandum outlining its demands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-bloc-huddle-leaders-to-meet-virtually-on-cec-row-sir-irregularities-on-agenda/articleshow/135107949.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-bloc-huddle-leaders-to-meet-virtually-on-cec-row-sir-irregularities-on-agenda/articleshow/135107949.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T11:00:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135108563,imgsize-90910.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Stand for what's true': Priyanka Gandhi's emotional message for son Raihan after over 70 images removed from exhibition]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/stand-for-whats-true-priyanka-gandhis-emotional-message-for-son-after-over-70-images-removed-from-exhibition/articleshow/135107661.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135107661.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/stand-for-whats-true-priyanka-gandhis-emotional-message-for-son-after-over-70-images-removed-from-exhibition/articleshow/135107661.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/stand-for-whats-true-priyanka-gandhis-emotional-message-for-son-after-over-70-images-removed-