imes.com/india/tricolor-row-what-happened-at-priyanka-gandhis-son-raihans-exhibition-at-bikaner-house-controversy-explained/articleshow/135105157.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135105157.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tricolor-row-what-happened-at-priyanka-gandhis-son-raihans-exhibition-at-bikaner-house-controversy-explained/articleshow/135105157.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tricolor-row-what-happened-at-priyanka-gandhis-son-raihans-exhibition-at-bikaner-house-controversy-explained/articleshow/135105157.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T08:37:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135105657,imgsize-86668.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kuwait-flagged tanker carrying 21 Indian seafarers hit by projectile in Strait of Hormuz; all safe]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kuwait-flagged-tanker-carrying-21-indian-seafarers-hit-by-projectile-in-strait-of-hormuz-all-safe/articleshow/135104277.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135104277.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A Kuwait-flagged oil product tanker, M/T Al Dasma, was struck by an unidentified projectile in the Strait of Hormuz. All 21 Indian seafarers aboard the vessel were reported safe after the incident on October 21. This event follows previous attacks on vessels in the region, raising safety concerns for Indian mariners. The Indian government is in contact with ship management to ensure ongoing security measures.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kuwait-flagged-tanker-carrying-21-indian-seafarers-hit-by-projectile-in-strait-of-hormuz-all-safe/articleshow/135104277.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kuwait-flagged-tanker-carrying-21-indian-seafarers-hit-by-projectile-in-strait-of-hormuz-all-safe/articleshow/135104277.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T07:40:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135104431,imgsize-30954.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why are uninsured vehicles not part of crash relief scheme? Supreme Court]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/why-are-uninsured-vehicles-not-part-of-crash-relief-scheme-supreme-court/articleshow/135100900.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135100900.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Taking note that “Compensation to Victims (Interim Relief) Scheme, 2026” has not been notified or publicised, a bench of Justices JB Pardiwala and KV Viswanathan directed the govt to publicise it to ensure awareness. People must be made aware of their right to seek interim compensation, it said. Union road transport ministry officials said the scheme will be notified as provided for under Central Motor Vehicle Act.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/why-are-uninsured-vehicles-not-part-of-crash-relief-scheme-supreme-court/articleshow/135100900.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/why-are-uninsured-vehicles-not-part-of-crash-relief-scheme-supreme-court/articleshow/135100900.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T03:32:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash and Amit Anand Choudhary</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135100935,imgsize-65866.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rosatom completes supply of engineered safety features actuation systems for Kudankulam N-plant units 3 and 4]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rosatom-completes-supply-of-engineered-safety-features-actuation-systems-for-kudankulam-n-plant-units-3-and-4/articleshow/135100849.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135100849.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In total, about 300 items of equipment were manufactured and delivered to the plant – four sets of ESFAS CS in accordance with the number of safety instrumentation and control trains, per each power unit featuring VVER-1000 reactors. ESFAS is the system that monitors the process parameters of a power unit when there is a deviation from normal operation conditions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rosatom-completes-supply-of-engineered-safety-features-actuation-systems-for-kudankulam-n-plant-units-3-and-4/articleshow/135100849.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rosatom-completes-supply-of-engineered-safety-features-actuation-systems-for-kudankulam-n-plant-units-3-and-4/articleshow/135100849.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T03:27:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Surendra Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135100874,imgsize-88042.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New norms for DL: Driving tutorial pass mark may rise to 75%, select licence services to be free]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-norms-for-dl-driving-tutorial-pass-mark-may-rise-to-75-select-licence-services-to-be-free/articleshow/135100709.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135100709.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Under the proposal, the safe-driving tutorial would have to last at least 30 minutes. The higher qualifying score of 70% is aimed at making the assessment more stringent. The draft also proposes a defined procedure for online applications to change driving licence particulars, including name and address. Licencing authorities would have to approve or reject applications for changes within 15 days, giving reasons for rejection.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-norms-for-dl-driving-tutorial-pass-mark-may-rise-to-75-select-licence-services-to-be-free/articleshow/135100709.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/new-norms-for-dl-driving-tutorial-pass-mark-may-rise-to-75-select-licence-services-to-be-free/articleshow/135100709.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-22T03:13:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135100720,imgsize-78908.cms"/></item></channel></rss>